EXT. GLACIER CAVE MOUTH - DAWN

A cathedral of blue ice. Cold fire glints along its roof. Wind keens through a crack as tall as a house. Snow whips past the entrance.

MORWENNA, 30s, a ranger in a hooded sealskin cloak with a spear, plants her feet at the cave mouth. IVAR, 70s, her mentor, white-bearded, leaning on a staff of driftwood, wheezes beside her.

MORWENNA
It's in there.

IVAR
It's always been in there.

She steps forward. The ice floor groans. A low note thrums from deep inside the cave, a note too big for a throat. They both freeze. The crack in the ceiling widens by a finger's width, and a skein of powder sifts down on their shoulders.

IVAR (CONT'D)
It knows you.

MORWENNA
It doesn't.

Out of the dark, an eye opens, pale as a moon, vertically slit. It regards them. Morwenna lifts her spear. Ivar grabs her wrist. They struggle, once, hard, until the spear clatters on the ice.

IVAR (CONT'D)
No weapons. Never weapons.

The eye blinks. The wind falls away. Morwenna looks at the old man, then at the eye, and slowly, she kneels.
